# Install

OKMate ships as a signed macOS app (with a CLI symlink) and as a crate you can
build from this repository. The same commands live in the
[README](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/blob/main/README.md); this page is
the product-site install guide.

## macOS app zip

Download `OKMate.zip` from the latest
[GitHub Release](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/releases/latest), unzip it,
and drag `OKMate.app` to `/Applications`.

Double-click opens the knowledge window (`view`) and restores
`~/.okmate/state` when present.

## Homebrew cask

Install the same release archive from the
[`koliyo/homebrew-okmate`](https://github.com/koliyo/homebrew-okmate) tap:

```sh
brew install --cask koliyo/okmate/okmate
```

Homebrew 6 requires an explicit trust step for third-party taps. The fully
qualified cask name taps `koliyo/okmate` and trusts only that cask. To trust
the whole tap instead:

```sh
brew tap koliyo/okmate
brew trust koliyo/okmate
brew install --cask okmate
```

The cask installs `OKMate.app` from that release `OKMate.zip` and uses
Homebrew’s `binary` stanza so `$(brew --prefix)/bin/okmate` (on Apple Silicon,
`/opt/homebrew/bin/okmate`) is a symlink to
`OKMate.app/Contents/MacOS/okmate`. That is the same crate binary: Finder or
no-args launch opens the window; `okmate check` and the other subcommands stay
CLI. Sparkle still runs only for the desktop window.

## CLI from this repository

From a clone of [github.com/koliyo/okmate](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate):

```sh
uv run --no-dev okmate-ops install cli
```

That puts `okmate` in `~/.local/bin`. For a one-off run without installing:

```sh
cargo run --no-default-features -p okmate -- check knowledge --profile strict
```

Release-build the CLI binary with `uv run --no-dev okmate-ops build`.

## macOS app from source

To assemble `OKMate.app` on a Mac (unsigned or ad-hoc unless you have the
release signing secrets):

```sh
uv run --no-dev okmate-ops package desktop
```

That packages the crate into an app bundle the same way a local maintainer
build does. It is not the signed GitHub Release zip and does not turn on
Sparkle against `releases/latest` unless you also follow the release path in
the README. Prefer the [Release zip](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/releases/latest)
or the Homebrew cask if you want the published, updating app.

## Autoupdate

The `.app` uses Sparkle. **Check for Updates…** and
`brew upgrade --cask okmate` both follow GitHub `releases/latest` (the same
channel as
[appcast.xml](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate/releases/latest/download/appcast.xml)).
The cask is marked `auto_updates` so Homebrew does not fight Sparkle. Neither
path rewrites `~/.okmate/` config, cache, or session.

After the second launch, Sparkle may ask to check automatically. An update
shows release notes and Install / Remind Me Later / Skip.

A `cargo install` or copied `okmate` binary on `PATH` does not self-update.
Use a new install, or the `.app`, for updates.

## After install

```sh
okmate check knowledge --profile strict --format terminal
```

`check`, `inspect`, `search`, and `build` take one root. If you have several
configured trees, list them first: [Multiple bundles](/docs/multiple-bundles/).
